==Battleground==
*1 [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>,
*6 [[Mistress Celeboodle]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*5 [[Scissoroo]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*2 [[Elder Sloth]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Scissoroo]] spawns after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Just like many [[Continuation Stage]]s from [[First Round (Expert)]] before it, this is another stage filled with lots of [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies, so any [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] cats, like [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] or [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] will be of use. This stage is also surprisingly easier than [[2nd Round: Dusk (Deadly)]].

Galactic Overseer Nyandam spawns near instantly with some Mistress Celeboodles, which give you a lot of money to start off with. You are then met by an Imperator Sael 10 seconds later who shouldn't be much of a problem, and Scissoroos start spawning not long after that, which shouldn't be that powerful either as long as they aren't de-synced, but you should usually be able to kill them in time before the next one appears. The main threats are the two Elder Sloths that gradually appear, but as long as you can sync their attacks to the best of your abilities they shouldn't do that much. After you have chipped down and killed all the backliners, you should be able to destroy the base and win.

